  "body": "A new guide page, `site/content/guide/model-to-machine.md`, from the draft reviewed with the user on 2026-11-25: the five steps (CAD, CAM, post, control, machine), conversational programming, kinds of CNC machines, 3D printing (out of scope, slicers), native vs neutral design files and Dutchman, machine file (.mch) vs post (.cps), tools and tool-library import/export, what goes in and out of CamCraft, machine + post pairs, which post to pick, at the machine, and how owners can help. Linked from the guide index and `machines.md`; new terms added to the glossary.\n\n## Review round 1 (head `74831cc7c`)\n\nThe review found four product claims that the tree does not support. Each claim is corrected. Three new tests in `crates/app/tests/docs_troubleshooting.rs` compare the page with `assets/machines/*.mch` and with the post table of `posting.md`.\n\n- The machine file section names **Show work envelope**. It does not say that the simulation shows a moving machine.\n- The Sodick ALC400G row says that the control is not confirmed and that the user selects the post.\n- The Makera Carvera is in the Mill row.\n- The Mach3 row names the five PCNC 770 and PCNC 1100 templates. Mach4 has its own row.\n\nThe tests are in the existing binary `docs_troubleshooting`. No new top-level test file is added.\n\n## How tested (final head `74831cc7c`, base `upstream/main` `267ee5096`)\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: 1 step, `app suites: docs_troubleshooting`, ok, 0 failed, 0 stalled.\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test docs_troubleshooting`: 5 passed, 0 failed.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --test docs_troubleshooting -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- The first gate run stalled in sccache on this host. The second run had `CAMCRAFT_NO_SCCACHE=1` and is the result above.\n\nPin proof: with the page of head `6a15b91dd`, these three tests FAIL. With the fixed page, they pass.\n\n- `model_to_machine_claims_no_moving_machine_in_simulation`\n- `model_to_machine_pairs_agree_with_posting_and_machine_files` (the glob `tormach-pcnc*.mch`; with only the Sodick row reverted, it fails on the missing \"Select the post manually\")\n- `model_to_machine_kinds_agree_with_machine_files` (`makera-carvera.mch` is in the row \"Router\")\n\nHeavy lanes: not run. The diff has one docs page and one docs test. It reaches no motion, sim, post, geometry or operation code.\n\nGoldens moved: not applicable. The diff reaches no recorded program, and the example catalog suites were not run for that reason.\n\nScreenshots: not applicable. The diff changes no `crates/ui` code.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- `zola build` and `zola check` on the fixed head. This session cannot start `zola`. The reading of the first head was 52 pages, 0 orphans. The fix adds one link, `@/guide/check-and-post/posting.md#post-processors`, which the page already uses in two other places.\n- The deployed site (it regenerates at the next cut).\n\nChangelog: none\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nFixes #4053\n",
